# IPL-era symbols for the P2500 boot EPROM and its RAM block.
#
#   ./p2500-emu --symbols symbols/ipl.sym --disasm 02DA:24
#
# Every name here is a fixed address of the boot ROM in roms/ipl.bin, or of
# the RAM block that ROM builds at $FE00-$FF2F, so unlike the CP/M-era
# names these can honestly be written down. Source: the ROM disassembly and
# the decoded RAM map in the research notes' TODO.md ("Reference: RAM
# addresses", IPL era). An address whose meaning is only a guess is not
# listed; a dump of $FE00-$FEFF at a breakpoint is still the artifact to
# read when one of these is not enough.
#
# Fingerprint, so `--symbols auto` can recognise this build without
# being told which disk is in the drive:
# The EPROM as the CPU sees it at $0000, NOT as a ROM image: that makes
# the rule self-expiring, which is what this file needs. Every name here
# is true exactly while the IPL owns the machine - once CBIOS banks the
# EPROM out of $0000-$0FFF and builds its own IM2 table over $FE00, both
# halves of this file are stale, and so is the fingerprint.
# match 0000:0400:1C8DB59E
#
# Format: ADDR NAME, hex, one per line. $ or 0x prefix optional, : or =
# accepted in place of the space, # and ; start a comment.

# ---- ROM entry points
0000 RESET
0003 DISPATCH
0100 COLDBOOT
014D GIVEUP
01EB VECT.COPY
01FB VECT.SRC
02DA DISPATCH.body
0333 REQ.SUBMIT
03E3 ISR.PRO1
0422 DISPATCH.TAB
043E ID0.DRIVEPREP
0498 FDC.IDLECHK
059C ID4.READDATA
06C6 BUSYWAIT1
0752 ISR.PRO2
0798 BUSYWAIT2
1000 BOOTSEC
4A00 SEC0.TARGET

# ---- the RAM block the IPL builds
FE00 IM2.TABLE
FE0A DEV.DISPATCH
FE19 REQ.BLK1
FE45 REQ.BLK2
FE59 REQ.BLK3
FE5E REQ.BLK4
FE83 DPB.IPL
FE84 DONE.CB
FE88 SPT
FE89 SECSIZE.N
FE90 TRACK.MUL
FE93 MODE.FLAG
FE94 REQ.COPY
FE9A SEC.COUNT
FE9C DMA.BUFADDR
FE9E REQ.PTR
FEA0 PIOA.VEC
FEA2 FDC.CMDBUF
FEAC FDC.RESULT
FEB3 DMA.TEMPL
FEC9 TRAMPOLINE
FECC DONE.TRAMP
FECF DONE.STATUS
FED5 BUSY.FLAG
FED6 DRIVE.MODE
FED8 PIOA.SHADOW
FED9 CYL.CACHE
FEDD FDC.OPCODE
FF26 SAVED.SP
